    effort: 'L',
    impact: 'High — full audit found 5 independent regime classifiers: (1) paper_trading_engine US (SPY/VIX, 4h cache, fails to "choppy"), (2) paper_trading_engine HK (HSI dual-SMA + breadth), (3) decision-engine (own SPY/VIX re-fetch, 15min cache, hardcoded non-configurable VIX thresholds, different CHOPPY rule, fails to "neutral" — the OPPOSITE fail-safe from #1), (4) ml-prediction\'s HMM overlay (4-state Gaussian, consumed only by #1), (5) signal-engine\'s own classifier (3-4 state bull/high_vol/bear/unknown vocabulary from Fear&Greed, stamped into every signal\'s reasons, with its own separate HK sub-classifier making it effectively 6). These provably disagreed at the same instant: different cache TTLs, different vocabularies, different failure defaults, different math for the same state name. A portfolio could be gated risk_off live while the BUY-alert emailer read a bull regime baked into a signal from hours earlier.',
    what: 'Supersedes/expands T232-REGIME-DUPLICATION (which only named 2 of the 5). Found during the 2026-07-03 deep logic review.',
