    implementedNote: 'UPDATE 2026-08-04 — closed a real, separate cost/latency gap this item\'s own comment history already flagged but left unfixed: _fetch_market_regime() (US) was called fresh — a real yfinance download of SPY/QQQ/VIX/VIX9D/IWM/MDY plus full reclassification — on EVERY _refresh_5m tick during ALL US market hours, with zero debounce. _regime_cache/_regime_cache_ts existed only as a 4-hour FAILURE fallback inside the except block, never as a rate limiter for the normal happy path. This was a real asymmetry: _fetch_hk_market_regime() already had a 30-minute freshness check at its own top (added earlier, with its own T237-REG1/REG2 bug-fix history proving it safe in production) — the US classifier never got the equivalent treatment. Fixed by adding the IDENTICAL 1800-second (30-minute) freshness check to the top of _fetch_market_regime(), reusing HK\'s own already-proven TTL rather than inventing a new number. Confirmed this doesn\'t sacrifice real responsiveness: the function\'s own _REGIME_HYSTERESIS_TICKS mechanism already requires 2 consecutive classifications (~10 min at the 5-min refresh cadence) before any state CHANGE takes effect, so a 30-minute data-freshness window is comfortably conservative relative to that existing guarantee. 5 new tests (test_regime_fetch_debounce.py), all adversarially verified. A real test-design mistake was self-caught and fixed along the way: the first version of these tests used a fake yfinance.download() that RAISED an exception to signal "was this called" — which accidentally routed through the function\'s own SEPARATE, pre-existing exception-fallback logic (the 4-hour-cache-or-choppy-default path), masking whether the NEW debounce check or the OLD exception handler produced the passing result — 3 of 5 tests still passed even with the debounce fix completely reverted, the exact "still passes after sabotage" red flag this repo\'s own testing discipline treats as a finding in its own right. Fixed by rebuilding the fake with a real-shaped, SUCCEEDING multi-ticker DataFrame instead of one that raises, cleanly isolating the debounce check from the unrelated fallback path — re-verified the sabotage is now correctly caught by all 3 previously-blind tests. Full 777-test market-data suite green after every revert; pyflakes clean (confirmed via git stash that all 3 pre-existing warnings predate this change). HK\'s own classifier, decision-engine\'s pass-through, signal-engine\'s intentionally-separate vocabulary, and ml-prediction\'s HMM overlay are all unchanged by this fix — purely a cost/latency debounce on the US classifier\'s own happy path, not a behavioral change to any regime classification logic itself.',
