    fix: 'Fixed 2026-07-07 — picked option (2) from the three the tracker listed (auto-trigger a refresh when a new stock is added) as the actual root-cause fix, rather than (1) a gate workaround or (3) a universe-definition change that wasn\'t actually broken. Added _trigger_new_stock_refresh(symbol, market) to admin.py, registered as a SECOND BackgroundTasks.add_task() immediately after the existing ingest_symbol task in both add_stock code paths (new stock AND re-adding an existing one). FastAPI runs background tasks sequentially in registration order, so this only fires once price-history ingestion has actually completed — no explicit chaining/polling needed. Scoped the refresh to just the new stock\'s market (not a full-universe rescan) via the existing per-market /rankings/refresh and /signals/refresh endpoints, matching the pattern _weekly_full_refresh already uses in scheduler.py. Reused the existing _service_token() helper from scheduler.py (imported lazily inside the function body, not at module load, to avoid any risk of a circular import between admin.py and scheduler.py — scheduler.py already imports from api/routes.py) rather than duplicating JWT-minting logic in admin.py.\n\nCompile-checked (3.12, matching the market-data container exactly). Verified live on local dev: confirmed the module loads cleanly on a full container restart (no circular import); could not safely exercise the full authenticated HTTP endpoint without fabricating a real admin credential (the only real admin user is the actual production username), so instead imported the exact module path the running app itself uses (src.api.admin, matching main.py\'s `uvicorn src.main:app` entrypoint) and called _trigger_new_stock_refresh(\'DT\', \'US\') directly — completed with no exception, logged add_stock.refresh_triggered, and confirmed via ranking-engine/signal-engine\'s own logs that both refresh calls landed and did real work (47 rankings persisted, signals refreshed).',
