    what: 'The original implementation ran its own live, unbounded fundamentals_snapshot query (ORDER BY snapshot_date DESC LIMIT 8, no date filter) and broadcast the result to every historical training row regardless of that row\'s own date — the exact bias class already fixed for recommendation_mean itself via a point-in-time snapshot join, but missed for this derived feature. Removed rather than left broken, per the module\'s own T237-ML2 comment.',
    fix: 'Reimplemented using the ALREADY-LOADED fund_snapshots list (the same data recommendation_mean\'s own correct PIT join already uses) — a .rolling(window=8, min_periods=2) applied directly on the recommendation_mean SERIES (sorted by snapshot_date) produces a per-snapshot delta, which is then merge_asof(direction="backward")\'d onto training rows exactly like every other PIT column, so a row can only ever see snapshots at or before its own date. Thresholded to the same +-0.15 bands as the live T220-F signal in signals.py. A second, previously-undiscovered gap found while reimplementing this: fund_snapshots was never wired into the inference_mode=True call site at all (only training), so even a correct reimplementation would have silently stayed NaN forever at live prediction time — fixed by adding a _load_fund_snapshots(symbol) call to the inference call site, computed unconditionally (not gated behind not inference_mode like the other PIT columns) since a live-prediction row IS "today," so seeing the full snapshot history through today is genuinely safe, not lookahead.',
