    implementedNote: 'DONE 2026-08-18. A real, session-poisoning bug self-caught during test-writing, not shipped: the first version had compute_kscore() do _active_weights = _load_active_weights() with no dict() copy — but _load_active_weights()\'s own fallback paths originally returned the module-level _WEIGHTS object DIRECTLY, and compute_kscore() mutates its local copy via del a few lines later. The very first call with any factor missing would have permanently deleted that key from the real _WEIGHTS dict, corrupting every later call in the same process. Caught when the pre-existing test_kscore.py::test_kscore_in_range — which never touches Redis mocking at all — started raising a real KeyError when run in the same pytest session as this feature\'s new tests, confirmed via git stash to NOT happen on unmodified code. Fixed defensively at BOTH layers: _load_active_weights() now always returns dict(_WEIGHTS) on every fallback path, AND compute_kscore() wraps the call in dict(...) too. 31 new tests total (test_kscore_weight_override.py, test_kscore_weight_sweep.py) — the pure candidate-generation/recompute/redistribution/cross-sectional-EV functions are directly behaviorally tested (no source-text extraction needed, they take plain data); the endpoint\'s own heavy-DB-dependency wiring is covered by source-text regression checks matching this test suite\'s own established proportionate-testing convention. Adversarially verified 6 sabotage/revert cycles, all caught: the mutation bug at both layers (5 tests + 2 dedicated mutation-safety tests), the ev_lift<=0 rejection, the router ordering (kscore_weights_status moved after /{symbol} — caught with a real index-comparison failure), the None-factor exclusion (caught with a real TypeError, not just a mismatch), and the top-decile sort direction (caught by correctly detecting the WORST stock\'s return being selected instead of the best). Full 61-test ranking-engine suite green modulo the ONE pre-existing, unrelated test_kscore_in_range failure (confirmed via git stash to predate this session — asserts 0<=v<=100 on a factor that\'s legitimately None by design). pyflakes clean (both remaining warnings confirmed pre-existing via git stash). See .claude/CLAUDE.md "T288-KSCORE-WEIGHT-SWEEP" for the full writeup.',
