    fix: 'DONE (this entry IS the deliverable) — full narrative (per-category justification, what this system does better than all 4 competitors, what\'s missing that Tier 11 didn\'t already cover, and a direct answer to "would a real trader trust this with real money today") is in AUDIT_REPORT_TIER234_2026-07-04.md Section A. Two things this system does better than all four: (1) an outcome-based confidence calibration exposed to the end user — none of the four competitors show a reliability diagram of their own rating/signal accuracy; (2) a real, config-driven gate/sizing engine with ~20 named, visible suppression reasons on paper-gates.tsx — closer to a live risk-management rulebook than anything the four competitors expose. Five concrete gaps identified beyond Tier 11: no point-in-time data-integrity guarantee for backtests (survivorship bias already documented as a known limitation — see aud14-survivorship/t17-survivorship-bias, CORRECTED 2026-07-05 to reflect this has actually REGRESSED, not "partially fixed" as previously claimed), no third-party-auditable signal track record, no macro/rates/cross-asset context feeding regime detection (SPY+VIX+Fear&Greed only), and no confidence-interval/sample-size weighting on any headline stat (a 62% win rate on 40 signals displays identically to 62% on 4,000).\n\nCORRECTION (2026-07-05): the original "zero options-derived signals" claim was WRONG — GET /stocks/{symbol}/options-flow (market-data/src/api/routes.py:1858) genuinely computes cp_ratio/sentiment/unusual-activity/per-contract is_whale (premium > $500K), surfaced to the frontend and partially read by signal generation (signals.py:504, sentiment+cp_ratio only). Accurate gap: no IV/skew as a standalone signal, and per-contract whale/unusual-activity detail is DISPLAY-ONLY — does not currently influence signal confidence or position sizing, only the aggregate sentiment ratio does. See docs/AUDIT_REPORT_TIER234_2026-07-04.md\'s Part 1 correction note for detail.\n\nCROSS-LINK (2026-07-05, per user request to connect ratings to actionable tracker items): charting 3/10 → T230-CHARTING-DRAWING-TOOLS (no drawing tools/custom indicators, the single biggest driver of the low score); screening 5/10 → T230-DATA-OPTIONS-CHAIN (no options chain at all) and the lack of any screener-backtest-replay feature (no existing tracker item — would need a new one if prioritized); backtesting rigor 6/10 (docked partly for "no visible slippage/commission drag separate from live paper trading") → T230-BACKTESTING-MULTISYMBOL (multi-symbol/portfolio-level backtest, closest existing item, though it doesn\'t fully cover the slippage-visibility gap either — a new item may be warranted); the "zero options-derived signals" and "no macro/rates/cross-asset context" gaps have NO existing tracker item at all (checked T230-DATA-STREAMING-QUOTES and searched for macro/yield/rates items — none found) — these are genuinely new, unfiled gaps, not yet actionable without their own tracker entries; the "no confidence-interval/sample-size weighting on headline stats" gap is PARTIALLY addressed already by T232-OC5\'s calibration work (SignalCard now shows "n=34" next to win rate per that fix) but the gap specifically about PORTFOLIO-level headline stats (Sharpe/win-rate on the paper-portfolio page) showing no n-based uncertainty band is still open and unfiled.',
