    fix: 'Fixed 2026-07-07 — added rvol to the Screener\'s merged Row type, computed inline during the existing rankings/signals/prices merge (rvol = prc.volume / prc.avg_volume, undefined if either is missing) — no new fetch, no new backend endpoint. Wired it into the existing filter/sort/column machinery by mirroring the pre-existing vol_ratio (avg5d/avg20d, a different metric already on this page) field-for-field: added minRvol to DEFAULT_FILTERS, a filter predicate, a "rvol" SortKey + comparator, a NumInput ("Min RVOL"), a conditionally-shown sortable column (only rendered when the filter is active, same UX as Vol Ratio), and a "Unusual Vol Today 🔥" quick-filter chip (minRvol=1.5) next to the existing "Vol Surge ⚡" chip. Reused the exact 1.5x/2.0x thresholds and amber/red color convention already established by the stock-detail-page RVOL chip for consistency — no new copy or threshold invented. Did not touch the CSV export (vol_ratio isn\'t in it either, so adding only rvol would have been inconsistent scope beyond this fix).\n\nType-checked clean (tsc --noEmit). Verification is partial: no headless-browser tool was available in this environment, so the RVOL column/filter/chip were not visually confirmed interactively in a real browser. What was verified: the dev server compiled the page with zero errors (367 modules, only a pre-existing unrelated viewport-meta warning) and served GET /screener with 200; the new code is a field-for-field mirror of the pre-existing, already-working vol_ratio pattern (same conditional rendering, same filter/sort wiring shape), which is what building it that way was for. Recommend a quick manual click-through in a real browser before considering this fully closed.',
