    what: 'The previous session (MD-HKCONNECT1) found the only free per-stock alternative — the akshare Python library\'s stock_hsgt_individual_em() — and deliberately deferred it as "an HTML scrape, not a clean API, with a known recent bug." A prompted re-investigation (triggered by 3 real DQ check failures — congress_trades, earnings_events, hk_connect_flows — surfaced via a data-quality alert email) re-examined this specific claim rather than accepting the prior deferral at face value: read akshare\'s own source code and found stock_hsgt_individual_em() is NOT an HTML scrape at all — it\'s a single plain requests.get() against a documented Eastmoney JSON API (datacenter-web.eastmoney.com/api/data/v1/get, reportName=RPT_MUTUAL_STOCK_HOLDRANKS). Installed akshare locally and called it live against 2 real HK stocks (00700.HK Tencent, 09988.HK Alibaba) — both returned genuine, day-to-day changing holdings data through the current date (2026-07-13), with no crash, contradicting the "known recent bug" — that GitHub issue (#6193) may have described a different akshare version, a different code path, or since been fixed upstream; either way it does not reproduce today. Also checked AAStocks.com per a direct user question — confirmed AAStocks has the same aggregate-only limitation as HKEX/Eastmoney\'s official pages (the underlying constraint is mainland exchanges\' 2024-08-19 disclosure-rule change, which killed per-stock TRANSACTION net-buy/sell data industry-wide — this Eastmoney report is a HOLDINGS snapshot, a genuinely different, still-live disclosure, which is why it still works).',
    fix: 'Called the underlying Eastmoney endpoint directly via httpx (already a dependency) rather than adding the full akshare package, which pulls in py-mini-racer (a bundled V8 JS engine), akracer, lxml, and other heavy dependencies for what is, under the hood, one HTTP GET with fixed query params. Rewrote hk_connect.py\'s _fetch_southbound_stock() around this endpoint: symbol codes need Eastmoney\'s 5-digit zero-padded format (00700.HK), not HKEX\'s 4-digit convention (0700) — confirmed live via a direct comparison (the old format returns 0 rows against this API). Maps ADD_MARKET_CAP (the day-over-day change in Stock Connect holding value, already priced at that day\'s close) directly to net_buy_hkd — a legitimate net-flow-direction proxy, though buy_hkd/sell_hkd stay None since this report can\'t split gross buy vs. sell like the old (dead) HKEX endpoint claimed to. Uses the report\'s OWN TRADE_DATE field per row, not the sync job\'s run date — applying the exact lesson just learned from the earnings_events fetched_at bug (same session): a daily snapshot report may not have a same-day row yet, and stamping it with "today" regardless would silently make the table look fresher than the underlying data really is.',
