    impact: 'Medium — found via a comprehensive multi-agent sweep of all 11 services specifically hunting for more instances of the EI-CONGRESS1/MD-CONGRESS1/MD-HKCONNECT1 pattern (external API silently degraded, broad except swallowing into an empty/fallback return with zero visibility). fetch_macro_features()\'s exception handler and empty-result fallback both returned silently with no logging at all. Production logs showed 210+ "possibly delisted" yfinance errors in a single day (2026-07-09) with nothing at the application level surfacing that macro features (SPY/VIX/HSI — used by every ML model\'s feature vector) had silently fallen back to a stale Redis cache. Unlike the other 3 fixes in this pattern, the underlying source (yfinance) is NOT dead — confirmed 0 occurrences of the error in the 6 hours following the spike, so this was transient (likely rate-limiting), not a persistent outage. Still a real gap: a genuinely prolonged outage would have been just as invisible as the other 3 bugs were before this pattern was recognized.',
    title: 'ML-MACRO1: fetch_macro_features() silently swallowed yfinance/Redis failures with zero logging — same pattern as 3 other bugs this session, caught before it became a persistent outage',
    what: 'Found via a 4-way parallel sweep (one sub-agent per 2-3 services) specifically targeting this failure class after EI-CONGRESS1/MD-CONGRESS1/MD-HKCONNECT1 established it recurs. The sweep also flagged and I independently discarded one stale/incorrect claim (event-intelligence\'s routes.py falsely reported as stale — verified via checksum, live route check, and sec_filings row count that it was current and working, 43 rows with the most recent dated the same day). Everything else checked across all 11 services (decision-engine, strategy-engine, portfolio-optimizer, technical-analysis, signal-engine, ranking-engine, research-engine, event-intelligence, api-gateway, and the rest of market-data — news.py, hmm_regime.py, admin.py, etrade_broker.py, portfolio.py) either has adequate logging already or has no external dependency at all.',
    fix: 'Fixed 2026-07-09 — added log.warning() to the SPY/VIX fetch except branch, the spy.empty/vix.empty fallback branch, the HSI fetch except branch, and both _redis_save_macro/_redis_load_macro helpers (including a new warning when the Redis cache itself is empty, meaning there is no fallback data at all). Purely additive logging — no behavior change to the actual fallback logic (still correctly prefers a stale-but-real Redis cache over zero-filling macro features, which the existing docstring correctly explains would cause train/inference distribution shift).\n\nCompile-checked. Confirmed via docker logs that the original error spike (210+ occurrences) has since cleared to 0 in the following 6 hours, confirming this was transient rate-limiting rather than a dead endpoint — this fix is purely about visibility for the next time it happens, not a data-source replacement.',
    implementedNote: 'Done 2026-07-09 — found via a dedicated 4-way parallel sweep for more instances of the dead/silent-external-API pattern; the only new real finding among all 11 services checked.',
