    implementedNote: 'Fixed 2026-07-11, all 6. AUD232-046: meta_trainer\'s query now selects so.signal_direction and the feature vector appends a BUY/SELL indicator (1.0/0.0) alongside the existing sector/market_cap/horizon meta-features, so the model can learn direction-specific patterns instead of blending two populations with different documented base rates into one drifting label. predict_meta() gained a direction parameter (default "BUY", matching its only current caller — trainer.py\'s ensemble blend, which is BUY-only by construction since _load_outcome_features filters signal_direction=="BUY"); appended at the end of the vector so an existing production model bundle (trained pre-fix) keeps working unaffected until its next natural retrain, since non_const\'s saved indices still point at their original positions. AUD232-047: signal_accuracy()\'s bare pct_change>=0/<=0 rule and rolling_accuracy()\'s bare exit_>entry rule both now apply the same _OUTCOME_WIN_HURDLE_PCT (0.5%) cost hurdle evaluate_signal_outcomes uses (scaled ×100 for signal_accuracy since its pct_change is already in percentage points). AUD232-048/049: calibrate_ta_weights() rewritten to join SignalOutcome directly (same signal_direction=="BUY" + is_correct pattern as calibrate_conviction_weights in the same file) instead of independently re-deriving entry/exit prices via its own bisect lookup against a single fixed hold_days param — removed the now-dead hold_days query param (only caller, the scheduler\'s weekly job, passes no query params) and ~40 lines of duplicate price-lookup machinery. AUD232-050: added a `reliable` boolean (n >= _CONF_CAL_MIN_COUNT) to each by_direction bucket in outcomes/summary, so a consumer can tell when a diagnostic bucket has not reached the same reliability bar as the gated calibrated_win_rate shown on signal cards, instead of the two silently disagreeing with no indication which is trustworthy; wired a ⚠ marker + tooltip onto the by_direction table on /signal-accuracy. AUD232-051: added _SELL_THRESHOLD_FALLBACK=0.35 as the single source of truth in signals.py (there is no per-style sell_threshold in _STYLE_PROFILES to source from, unlike BUY, so a shared constant — not a fake per-style dict — is the correct fix); routes.py\'s outcomes_calibrate_apply now imports it instead of keeping its own hardcoded copy whose comment literally said "matches the hardcoded fallback in signals.py" as a manual-sync reminder. All touched files compile clean; frontend typechecks clean; market-data\'s 80-test suite unaffected (fixes are in signal-engine/ml-prediction, whose test suites are container-only — not runnable standalone in this host env, confirmed pre-existing via git stash, not something this change broke).',
