    implementedNote: 'Fixed 2026-07-11, both. AUD232-054: verified against real production stocks.sector distinct values (11 real values, including 6 stocks with sector=\'Financial\' and 2 with \'Consumer Defensive\') — added "Consumer Defensive": "XLP" to builder.py\'s SECTOR_ETF_MAP (Consumer Staples Select Sector SPDR, a real ETF ticker) and "Financial": 11 to meta_trainer.py\'s SECTOR_MAP (appended as a new ordinal value rather than renumbering — existing trained model bundles already encode sectors against the existing integers, and reordering would silently corrupt their learned sector coefficients; a brand-new ordinal for a previously-unseen sector is safe since old bundles simply never saw it during training, same as any new category value). Did not merge the two maps into one shared module as the fix text proposed — they serve genuinely different purposes (ETF-symbol lookup vs. ordinal encoding) and merging would be a bigger refactor than the actual bug (coverage drift) warrants; keeping them separate but coverage-synced (with a cross-referencing comment in each) is the lower-risk fix. AUD232-055: trainer.py\'s _load_outcome_features() now reads the module\'s own _HORIZON_BY_STYLE constant instead of an independent inline copy. Also fixed the 3rd copy this surfaced while checking whether the other "4 total copies" claim still held: ml-prediction/src/api/routes.py had its own separately-hardcoded (but currently in-sync) _HORIZON_BY_STYLE — exported the trainer.py constant via training/__init__.py and switched routes.py to import it instead, since both live in the same service and this consolidation was low-risk (no cross-service import needed). Left signal-engine\'s independent copy (a different service, would need a cross-service shared package) as the remaining, genuinely-deferred item. All 5 touched files compile clean.',
