    title: 'supertrend()\'s final_upper/final_lower band-carry logic never seeds itself once ATR first becomes non-NaN, so the entire supertrend line and trend direction get stuck at their NaN/initial values forever, for every symbol.',
    what: 'At i=period (e.g. i=10 with period=10), basic_upper[i] is finally a real number but final_upper[i-1] is still NaN (copied from basic_upper[i-1]). Both branches of the ternary `basic_upper[i] < final_upper[i-1] or close_v[i-1] > final_upper[i-1]` evaluate to False (any comparison against NaN is False), so the else-branch runs and sets final_upper[i] = final_upper[i-1] = NaN instead of adopting the fresh basic_upper[i] value. This NaN then propagates through every subsequent iteration via final_upper[i-1]/final_lower[i-1], meaning `st_line`/`supertrend` is 100% NaN for the full length of any input (verified with 400 synthetic bars: all 400 values NaN), and `trend` never leaves its initial +1, so `cross_up`/`cross_down` never fire even once. The GET /ta/{symbol}/indicators endpoint (routes.py lines 78-80) serves entirely-null supertrend/supertrend_trend to every caller, silently, with no exception.',
