    implementedNote: 'Fixed 2026-07-14. Independently reproduced the bug myself BEFORE trusting the audit\'s claim (per this session\'s established discipline of verifying high-severity findings against real code/data, not just accepting an automated report) — ran supertrend() against 400 synthetic OHLC bars and confirmed 100% NaN output, trend stuck at the initial +1, zero cross signals, exactly as claimed. Fix adds an explicit `if np.isnan(final_upper[i-1])` / `if np.isnan(final_lower[i-1])` branch that seeds directly from that bar\'s own basic_upper[i]/basic_lower[i] instead of falling through to the NaN-poisoned ternary. Re-ran the same 400-bar reproduction after the fix: supertrend is now NaN only for the correct 9-bar ATR warmup (period=10, min_periods=10), trend correctly alternates between +1/-1 (7 cross-ups, 8 cross-downs over 400 bars), matching a genuinely working indicator. Added 4 new regression tests to test_indicators.py (this module had ZERO supertrend test coverage before this fix) — non-NaN past warmup, trend not stuck, cross signals can fire, first-valid-bar seeds correctly. Adversarially verified by reverting to the original buggy code and confirming all 4 new tests correctly failed, then restoring the fix and re-confirming all 9 tests (4 new + 5 pre-existing) pass. Compiles clean.',
