    title: 'GET /signals/{symbol}?persist=true used a bare session.add(Signal(...)) with no ON CONFLICT handling — a same-day signal that genuinely changed value could raise an unhandled IntegrityError',
    what: 'If today\'s stored signal (e.g. from a scheduled _bulk_persist run) differs from the freshly recomputed one — a real price move, or this same function\'s own catalyst-nudge re-evaluation flipping HOLD->BUY/SELL a few lines above — the insert violates uq_signals_stock_horizon_day (stock_id, horizon, date_trunc(\'day\', ts)), an unhandled IntegrityError that 500s the whole request and rolls back every horizon\'s signal in the same commit, not just the one that changed. Found while re-deriving findings lost to an earlier spend-limit interruption; independently verified by confirming the real unique index exists in shared/db/models.py and that _bulk_persist() (the scheduled path) already uses a real ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE upsert specifically to avoid this exact class of failure — the manual-refresh GET path was the one call site that never received the same treatment.',
