    implementedNote: 'Fixed 2026-07-14: replaced the same-day-guard-then-bare-insert with the identical INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (stock_id, horizon, date_trunc(\'day\', ts)) DO UPDATE upsert _bulk_persist() already uses (CAST() instead of ::type to avoid the SQLAlchemy text() cast-binding ambiguity, BUG-6), so this path can no longer violate the index regardless of whether today\'s stored value matches. Added tests/test_signal_get_path_upsert.py (4 tests) — since routes.py can\'t be imported directly here (from common.jwt_auth import ... fails against the blanket common stub), these verify the actual upsert SQL text extracted directly from source: real ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE (not a bare insert), targets the correct index, uses CAST() not ::type, and updates ts = NOW(). Adversarially verified: reverting to the same-day-guard-plus-bare-insert made all 4 tests fail exactly as expected; restoring the fix passed all 11 tests in the reachable suite (test_signal_generator.py has a pre-existing, unrelated import error not caused by this change).',
