    fix: 'ALTER TABLE per the CLAUDE.md create_all()-gap discipline (create_all() only creates new tables, never widens existing columns) — widened research_rec to String(32), applied directly against production Postgres, not just the SQLAlchemy model.',
    implementedNote: 'Fixed 2026-07-14: widened `SignalOutcome.research_rec` from String(16) to String(32) in shared/db/models.py, with margin above the longest current real value (10-char "STRONG BUY"). Since this is a column WIDTH change on an existing, already-populated table, create_all() would not apply it — ran `ALTER TABLE signal_outcomes ALTER COLUMN research_rec TYPE VARCHAR(32);` directly against production Postgres (per this repo\'s standing create_all()-gap discipline), then synced shared/db/ to every service container per the stale-shared-db-copy discipline (signal-engine + every other service that reads this table). Added tests/test_signal_outcome_research_rec_width.py (3 tests) using a real in-memory SQLite table loaded via importlib. Adversarially verified: reverting to String(16) made the column-width assertion test fail (16 not >= 32) — note SQLite itself doesn\'t enforce varchar length at the storage layer, so the insert-succeeds tests alone wouldn\'t have caught a reversion; the explicit width-assertion test is what catches it, matching the real Postgres enforcement this fix targets. Restoring the fix passed all 3 tests (14/14 full reachable suite). Verified live: triggered a real evaluate_signal_outcomes() run in production and confirmed zero StringDataRightTruncation errors, with signal_outcomes rows containing "INSUFFICIENT DATA" now persisting successfully.',
