    fix: 'Added an "Anchored VWAP" entry to the existing Volume Profile toolbar dropdown. One click (not two, unlike Fixed Range VP\'s start+end pair) sets anchoredVwapIdx via its own separate, lightweight useEffect (chart.subscribeClick(), unsubscribed on cleanup — same pattern as Fixed Range VP/drawing tools, not the main chart-rebuild effect). The click snaps to the nearest T252-AUTO-SWING-PIVOTS pivot within 3 bars too — an anchor is far more useful planted on a real swing high/low than an arbitrary bar a few pixels off. Rendering reuses the exact same computeVwap() function, just fed activePrices.slice(anchoredVwapIdx) instead of the full array, drawn as a second, visually distinct line series (solid cyan, vs. the existing dashed violet rolling VWAP) starting at the anchor bar\'s own time.',
    implementedNote: 'Done 2026-07-19. Manually verified the slicing logic against a hand-computed fixture (a 4-bar series where the anchored VWAP starting at bar 2 correctly resets to bar 2\'s own typical price, 115, and diverges from the full-window VWAP at the same point, 107.2 vs 115) — confirms the anchor genuinely changes the calculation rather than just changing which line is drawn. A pre-existing, unrelated bug was found and fixed along the way: this repo has no live Tailwind pipeline (no tailwind.config.js/postcss.config.js — same root cause already documented for ToolbarDropdown.tsx\'s transparent-dropdown bug), and Fixed Range VP\'s own click-picking status pill (bg-violet-900/40, border-violet-500/50, text-violet-300) and the VWAP legend swatch (border-violet-400) both used classes with zero matching rule in globals.css, silently no-oping — fixed both to inline styles while touching this exact code, using the new Anchored VWAP pill/swatch as the reference for what these were SUPPOSED to look like. No dedicated test file exists for this change (computeVwap lives inline in PriceChart.tsx, which has no test file — the same seam gap as every other PriceChart.tsx-only change in this repo); full 63-test frontend vitest suite (unaffected, none of it touches PriceChart.tsx directly), typecheck, and a full next build all green.',
