    fix: 'Chose client-side port over a new backend endpoint: Fixed Range VP\'s click-snap needs pivots indexed against the EXACT SAME activePrices[] array the click handler already reads bar indices from (a round-trip endpoint would need its own index-alignment logic against a potentially-different bar window) — matching how volumeProfile.ts/indicators.ts already do local computation instead of adding backend round-trips for chart-only features. New frontend/src/lib/swingPivots.ts: detectSwingPivots() ports _find_pivots()\'s exact algorithm, detecting on high/low (not close) to match trendlines.py\'s own T247-TA-CLUSTERPIVOTS-CLOSE-HIGH-MISMATCH fix (a "swing high/low" is the bar\'s actual extremum, not wherever it closed) — deliberately NOT reusing detect_trendlines()\'s close-based pivots, which serve a different purpose (trendline fitting, not swing-extreme marking). nearestPivot() snaps an arbitrary bar index to the closest real pivot within a tolerance. PriceChart.tsx: new "Swing Pivots" toggle in the Indicators dropdown (off by default, daily-only) renders small dot markers via candles.setMarkers() — merged into the SAME setMarkers() call as the existing signal-transition arrows rather than a second call, which would have silently clobbered whichever ran first. Fixed Range VP\'s click handler now always snaps the raw clicked bar index to the nearest pivot within 3 bars (nearestPivot(swingPivots, rawIdx, 3)) regardless of whether the marker overlay itself is toggled on — the snap benefit shouldn\'t require turning on the visual.',
    implementedNote: 'Done 2026-07-19. 10 new tests in swingPivots.test.ts covering empty/too-short input, correct high/low pivot identification on a zigzag fixture, no false positives on a strictly monotonic run, the +-order edge exclusion, ts pass-through, and nearestPivot\'s within-tolerance/out-of-range/tie-break/empty-list behavior. Directly cross-checked against the REAL Python _find_pivots() (not just internally-consistent TS expectations, per this repo\'s own established discipline for hand-translated formulas) by running the identical zigzag fixture through both `_find_pivots(pd.Series(highs), order=3)` and detectSwingPivots() — both produced the identical pivot index (high at idx 4, low at idx 8), confirming the port is faithful rather than plausible-looking. Full 52-test frontend vitest suite, typecheck, and a full next build all green.',
