    implementedNote: 'Phase 1 fully done. FUTURES half done 2026-07-22 — new _fetch_overnight_futures() (one bulk yf.download() of ES=F/NQ=F/YM=F/RTY=F, Redis-cached 60s) folded into the existing 8:00 send_premarket_brief as a new "Overnight Futures" section, US-only-gated (matches sections 1/3), reporting the measured overnight change with explicit "not a prediction of whether it holds" framing. 13 new tests (test_overnight_futures_brief.py), adversarially verified.\n\nPREMARKET-GAPPERS half done 2026-07-23 — the missing ingest job was built: new _refresh_premarket_5m() (services/market-data/src/services/scheduler.py) registered as two cron jobs covering the US 4:00-9:25 ET premarket window (hands off cleanly to the existing us_5m_intraday\'s own 9:30 start, no double-fire), deliberately NOT reusing _refresh_5m() as-is since that function also unconditionally runs paper-trading/SHORT-intraday checks tuned for regular hours — the premarket job does the ingest only. New _fetch_premarket_gappers() query (gap % = today\'s latest PRE-session 5m close vs. yesterday\'s REGULAR daily close, same row_number()-per-stock_id window-function pattern already established in routes.py\'s _latest_prices_from_db()), folded into send_premarket_brief() as a 5th "Premarket Movers" section. 19 new tests (test_premarket_gappers.py, real-in-memory-SQLite technique), adversarially verified (2 sabotage cycles — removing the US-market filter, removing the PRE-session filter — both caught, plus a real test-writing mistake of my own caught and fixed: an early test checked the new ingest function\'s FULL source including its own docstring, which legitimately names the two forbidden calls in prose while explaining why they\'re skipped, producing a false failure against correct code). Full 486-test market-data suite (up from 432) green.\n\nPhase 2 (options-flow snapshot persistence) done 2026-07-30 — new options_flow_snapshot.py module independently re-derives get_options_flow()\'s exact cp_ratio/sentiment/whale math from a fresh yfinance option-chain fetch (plus call/put premium totals the live endpoint doesn\'t already aggregate), new OptionsFlowSnapshot table (brand-new, create_all()-friendly, no migration needed), a new _bounded_options_flow_symbols() (PriceAlert-subscribed + top-20-by-K-Score US stocks, correctly excludes delisted/inactive per BUG-DELISTED-GENERATION-BLIND\'s established pattern) feeding a new 17:00 ET EOD compute job with per-symbol error isolation + a 2s rate-limit sleep, upserted idempotently. Folded into send_premarket_brief() as a 6th "Late-Day Options Flow" section reading ONLY already-persisted rows (zero live yfinance call in the brief path itself). 26 new tests across 2 files, adversarially verified (5 sabotage cycles — delisted/inactive filter removal, US-only filter removal, the US-only fetch gate, the nothing-to-report guard, and a real runtime TypeError caught by removing the None-safety guards on cp_ratio/sentiment rendering — all 5 caught correctly). Full 656-test market-data suite (up from 486) green. See .claude/CLAUDE.md\'s "Feature Reference: T257-OVERNIGHT-FLOW-BRIEF Phase 2" for full detail.\n\nPhase 3 (the "day layout" attention list) done 2026-07-30 — new pure _build_attention_list() scores each recipient\'s OWN watched symbols against the 4 already-computed Phase 1/2 inputs (premarket gap >=2.0%, notable options-flow sentiment or a real whale trade, earnings today, a market-wide high/critical macro release today), requiring >=2 hits before a symbol qualifies. Each qualifying symbol carries its own list of measured-fact reason strings — deliberately never a synthesized buy/sell verdict, per the design\'s own explicit rejection of duplicating direction calls the signal pipeline + T257-TOP3 already own with tracked accuracy. Computed per-recipient inside the send loop (the one section in this function that genuinely needs to be, since it scores each user\'s own symbol set, not a market-wide list); folded into send_premarket_brief_email() as a new "Today\'s Attention List" section. 23 new tests (test_attention_list.py), adversarially verified (4 sabotage cycles — loosening the >=2 threshold, removing the gap-threshold check, widening the notable-sentiments set, severing the email-wiring call — all caught correctly, including a real test-writing mistake of my own caught and fixed: an early test anchored on the function\'s own docstring mention before its real call site, the same class of bug already hit twice before in this item\'s own history). Full 679-test market-data suite (up from 656) green. See .claude/CLAUDE.md\'s "Feature Reference: T257-OVERNIGHT-FLOW-BRIEF Phase 3" for full detail. All 3 phases of this tracker item are now complete.',
