    fix: 'New standalone news-intelligence service (port 8011, FastAPI + AsyncIOScheduler, matching event-intelligence\'s scaffolding exactly): PR Newswire + Business Wire RSS pollers (GlobeNewswire dropped for Business Wire after the dead-URL finding; Business Wire\'s only public feed is a generic international firehose, ASCII-filtered to drop non-English noise), a SEC EDGAR real-time filing poller (8-K/4/SC 13D types), and a long-lived Alpaca WebSocket client with automatic reconnect-with-backoff. Ticker matching is deliberately UNIVERSE-AWARE, not a bare regex — extract_symbols() only ever matches against this app\'s own real Stock.symbol/Stock.name rows (loaded fresh, 15-min cached), and EDGAR filings resolve via an exact Stock.cik lookup — fixing the exact false-positive class that broke the original design. Headlines are classified (sentiment/materiality/category) via a batched Claude Haiku call, reusing the established _claude_sentiment()/_strip_markdown_fence() pattern. A material headline sets a 2-hour Redis hot-news flag per symbol, read by signal-engine\'s new _fetch_hot_news() and applied as a direction-aware compression in _apply_style_signal() (30% compression toward neutral for a BUY-leaning signal on MATERIAL NEGATIVE news only — never boosts a SELL/HOLD back to BUY on positive news, a suppression-only gate matching the original design\'s own defensive intent, generalized beyond just gap-downs). Alpaca credentials are admin-configured via a new Settings page section (mirroring the Claude/DeepSeek key pattern exactly), stored in Redis via shared/common/ai_keys.py\'s new get_alpaca_credentials(), never in .env/files. New frontend /news page (symbol/material/source filters, 60s refresh) plus a new nav entry under Research.',
    implementedNote: 'Done 2026-07-27. New RealtimeNewsItem table (create_all()-friendly, no migration needed), (source, url, symbol) unique constraint for idempotent re-polling. Full test suite: 47 tests in the new service (tickers.py\'s universe-aware matching — including the exact EPS/CEO/AI/IPO/FDA false-positive regression case the original design failed on; rss_sources.py/edgar_source.py against real feedparser on constructed fixture XML/Atom, not live network calls; classify.py against a mocked httpx.Client, matching risk_agent.py\'s established Claude-test pattern; alpaca_source.py\'s pure message-parser; storage.py\'s hot-news Redis flag) plus 7 new signal-engine tests for the hot-news gate itself (compression direction, no-op on positive/neutral material news, no-op when already SELL-leaning, missing-sentiment-label handling). All adversarially verified via sabotage-and-confirm-failure — including a real near-miss caught mid-verification: the first substring-collision test fixture ("Camden"/"AMD") never actually exercised the word-boundary guard under sabotage, because bare-ticker matching is already case-sensitive and "Camden" (mixed case) never collides with the all-caps "AMD" pattern regardless — fixed by using a same-case adversarial fixture ("PYRAMDING"), re-verified the sabotage is now correctly caught. A real correctness bug was ALSO caught and fixed while writing edgar_source.py\'s own tests (not shipped): _fetch_one() built its headline using the query\'s own filing_type param ("8-K") instead of the ACTUAL parsed form from the entry title, meaning an 8-K/A amendment returned by an 8-K-type query would be silently mislabeled as a fresh "8-K filed" — fixed to use the regex\'s own parsed form group. Full frontend vitest suite (89 tests), typecheck, and a full next build all green throughout. Deliberately did NOT duplicate the T249 macro/earnings alert systems (CPI/NFP/GDP/FOMC releases, earnings dates/results) — this service is scoped to ad-hoc company headline news specifically, per direct clarification mid-build.',
