    fix: 'Add a monitor on the conviction_met -> fired ratio and alert when it collapses, so a future threshold change that zeroes the stream is caught immediately rather than silently.',
    implementedNote: 'FIXED 2026-08-14, per production log ratios confirmed 2026-08-05. Before this fix, neither the conviction gate\'s own pass count nor the actual-email-sent count was persisted anywhere outside a structlog line — there was no way to build a monitor at all without first creating the underlying counters.\n\nAdded two rolling 48h Redis counters (_incr_rolling_counter(), a plain INCR + "expire only on first write" idiom so a steady stream of increments never resets the window forever): _CONVICTION_MET_COUNTER_KEY incremented at the exact "signal_alert.conviction_met" log point inside check_signal_alerts(), _ALERT_FIRED_COUNTER_KEY incremented at the "signal_alert.fired" log point — but ONLY when current=="BUY", since exit/bearish transitions bypass the conviction gate entirely (see the function\'s own docstring) and counting them would understate the real conviction-met -> fired collapse this check exists to catch.\n\nWired into the existing _DQ_CHECKS/run_data_quality_checks() framework (the same declarative-check + dq_check:{name} Redis key + failing-list + email-on-failure machinery every other staleness check already uses) via a genuinely new `source: "ratio"` dispatch branch — every existing entry asks "is this data fresh enough," this one asks "did enough conviction-gated candidates actually turn into a real alert," so it computes its own ok/failing state independently rather than forcing a ratio into the age-based schema. min_denominator=20 (below this, the ratio isn\'t evaluated at all — an early-window sample of a handful of candidates producing 0 fires isn\'t yet a meaningful signal) and min_ratio=0.001 (0.1%, deliberately well below the real incident\'s own ~0.56% ratio — set to catch a future collapse to near-zero, not to second-guess how selective the gates are allowed to be by design).\n\nA real, separate bug caught and fixed in the same pass: send_data_quality_alert_email() hardcoded `f"max {c[\'max_age_hours\']:.0f}h"` with no None-guard — every existing _DQ_CHECKS entry always has a real max_age_hours, but the new ratio check\'s failing-check dict correctly has max_age_hours=None (there\'s no age concept for a ratio) plus a new optional `detail` string instead. Without the fix, ANY real ratio-check failure would have crashed the alert email itself with `TypeError: unsupported format string passed to NoneType.__format__` — caught by writing a dedicated test for exactly this case before it could ship, not found via a live failure.\n\nTests: 24 new cases across 2 files. test_conviction_fired_ratio_dq_check.py (12 cases) — _incr_rolling_counter()\'s TTL-set-once behavior, fail-silent-on-Redis-error; the ratio branch\'s below-floor/healthy/collapsed/missing-counter cases (using the real production incident\'s own 27/4824 ratio as the "healthy" fixture); the _DQ_CHECKS entry\'s shape (no query/job_name key); the counter-increment call sites\' wiring inside check_signal_alerts() including the BUY-only guard; and the email builder\'s None-safe rendering. All via exec()-extraction of the real source (scheduler.py can\'t be imported directly in this test environment — apscheduler isn\'t installed locally), matching test_dq_check_job_status_source.py\'s established technique — including wrapping the extracted ratio branch in a real `for` loop so its own `continue` statement stays syntactically valid outside its normal loop context, a genuinely new wrinkle this extraction technique hadn\'t hit before. A related, separately-scoped alerts-environment-gate fix (BUG-LOCALDEV-ALERTS-UNGATED, T270-DBSYNC-PROD-TO-LOCAL-WEEKLY\'s own Layer 1) added 12 more tests in test_alerts_env_gate.py in the same session.\n\nAdversarially verified 3 sabotage cycles, all caught and reverted: removing the min_denominator floor guard (caught 2 tests, one via a real ZeroDivisionError — confirming the guard prevents a genuine crash, not just a defensive nicety); disabling the ratio comparison (`ratio_ok = True` unconditionally, caught by the dedicated collapsed-ratio test); removing the email builder\'s None-safe guard (caught with the exact real TypeError described above). Full 1250-test market-data suite green (up from 1226); pyflakes clean (confirmed via git stash that every pre-existing warning predates this change).',
