    what: 'User reported "I have some earning alerts and today there are some earning released but I never got any alert." Traced live: check_earnings_reactions()/check_earnings_impact_alerts() both gate on EarningsEvent.eps_actual IS NOT NULL, populated only by event-intelligence\'s sync_todays_earnings() (every 15 min, 7am-9pm ET) calling yfinance\'s ticker.earnings_history/earnings_dates. Confirmed directly against yfinance for that day\'s actual reporters (NET, RGTI, TTGT, KGS): every one still showed "Reported EPS: NaN" hours after their scheduled report time — the real data genuinely hadn\'t landed in yfinance yet. Several OTHER symbols in the DB with a report_date of "today" (DDOG, AKAM, HWM, OSCR, IMVT, BKSY, QBTS) turned out to be stale/approximate forward-looking calendar estimates, not real same-day reporters at all — confirmed by finding their actual most-recent print was already resolved weeks earlier (e.g. DDOG\'s real Q2 print, dated 2026-06-30, already had eps_actual=0.65 from months ago). The pipeline itself was working correctly; the underlying data source was simply not fast enough for a real subset of cases.',
