    implementedNote: 'BUILT 2026-08-06. New check_early_earnings_news_alerts() (market-data/scheduler.py), same cadence/lock/recipient-scoping/dedup conventions as its siblings check_earnings_reactions()/check_earnings_impact_alerts() (reuses _earnings_alert_recipient_symbols(), the shared PriceAlert-OR-EarningsAlertSubscription merge). For each recipient-subscribed symbol whose most recent {yesterday,today}-dated EarningsEvent row still has eps_actual NULL (the core non-duplication guarantee — once the real number lands, the existing reaction alert already owns delivery for that symbol, so this early alert must stop firing), calls the ALREADY-EXISTING GET /news?symbol=X&since_hours=24 endpoint on news-intelligence and looks for the first item with category=="earnings". If found, sends a lightweight email with the raw headline — explicitly framed as "we spotted earnings news... not a confirmed result... follow-up alert once the numbers land," never implying a result that doesn\'t exist yet. Dedup: one email per (user, symbol, day) via Redis, set only after a successful send (matching the AUD266-DEDUP-KEY-SET-BEFORE-SEND fix already applied to every sibling alert in this file). Per-recipient send is wrapped in its own try/except (matching AUD266-PER-RECIPIENT-ISOLATION-NEVER-PROPAGATED). Zero new endpoints needed on news-intelligence\'s side — GET /news already returns `category` per item, exactly the field needed.\\n\\nTests: 16 new cases in services/market-data/tests/test_early_earnings_news_alert.py — _fetch_earnings_news_headline() is tested directly and behaviorally (extracted via exec() against a fake httpx.Client, since scheduler.py can\'t be imported directly in this test environment and httpx is stubbed as a bare MagicMock by conftest.py): finds the first earnings-classified item, returns None when absent/on a non-200/on a network exception, queries the correct symbol/endpoint, and returns the FIRST (not last) matching item per the API\'s own most-recent-first ordering. check_early_earnings_news_alerts() itself covered via source-text regression checks matching this repo\'s established convention for this class of function: recipient scoping reuses the shared helper (not a re-derived narrower query), the eps_actual-still-null guard is present, the dedup key is scoped per (user, symbol, day) and written only inside the successful-send branch, the send call is per-recipient isolated, _record_job_status fires on every exit path, the lock key/TTL and scheduler registration match the established pattern, and the email body explicitly frames this as a detection rather than a confirmed result.\\n\\nAdversarially verified 3 sabotage cycles, all caught and reverted: removing the eps_actual-still-null filter (caught by the dedicated non-duplication test); moving the dedup-key setex to BEFORE the send call, reintroducing the exact AUD266-DEDUP-KEY-SET-BEFORE-SEND bug class (caught by the dedicated ordering test with a real index-comparison failure); removing the per-recipient try/except entirely (caught — the test could no longer even find the expected try-block source pattern). Full 976-test market-data suite green after every revert (up from 960); pyflakes clean (4 pre-existing, unrelated warnings confirmed via git stash to predate this change, only line numbers shifted).\\n\\nNot built this pass: a genuinely faster same-day EDGAR-filing-to-EPS-number parse (the news feed only surfaces the headline/existence of the release, not structured actual-vs-estimate numbers — that still requires yfinance or a second structured data source); a cross-check against a second earnings-calendar API (Finnhub/Alpha Vantage/Zacks) to validate yfinance\'s own calendar-date field, which this investigation found can itself be stale/approximate for some symbols — a real, separate gap worth its own future pass.',
