    what: 'y_dir = (fwd_ret > 0) is a direction label and y_ret = fwd_ret is the raw signed forward return. compute_holdout_ev takes mean(y_ret[probs >= 0.60]) — correct ONLY if a high probability means "go long", but nothing in the gate enforces that. There is no sign check, no monotonicity check, and no win-rate check; MIN_HOLDOUT_SIGNALED_ROWS=10 is the only floor. The gate cannot distinguish "a better long signal" from "different-but-not-worse noise", because it only compares candidate EV to the BASELINE MODEL\'s EV on the same slice, never to the unconditional holdout mean.',
