    fix: 'New _hk_board_lot_size(price) helper — a DOCUMENTED, price-tier APPROXIMATION (mirroring HKEX\'s real practice of assigning smaller lots to higher-priced stocks), NOT the real per-symbol lot size, since no such data exists anywhere in this app\'s pipeline (checked: absent from yfinance Ticker.info, absent from the Stock model, no HKEX scrape exists — fetching real per-symbol lots would need a new data-source integration, out of scope for this fix). Applied by rounding shares DOWN to a whole multiple of the approximated lot size at both places _scan_for_entries() computes a fresh shares value for an HK candidate (right after the PT-C2 rounding, and again inside the max_position_pct cap branch, which re-derives shares fractionally). Rounding down only ever reduces risk relative to the risk-budget math, never exceeds it. A candidate whose risk budget does not cover even one whole lot rounds to shares=0, caught by the pre-existing FIN-07 `shares < 0.01` skip with no new skip branch needed — this is exactly "skip the entry if one lot exceeds the risk budget" from the original fix description.',
    implementedNote: 'FIXED 2026-08-10. Originally INVESTIGATED 2026-08-05 in response to HK SWING showing 0% win rate (0/4, -6611 P&L on 300k) — that investigation found the HK config overrides are all TIGHTER not looser, and the sizing math is currency-agnostic, so there was no scale bug; the board-lot gap was reported as the one concrete, confirmable HK-path defect rather than a manufactured cause for the win rate. New tests: services/market-data/tests/test_hk_board_lot_rounding.py (9 cases) — direct tests of _hk_board_lot_size() (boundary tiers, monotonic non-increasing lot size as price rises, rounding-down never exceeds the original risk budget, the exact "risk budget smaller than one lot rounds to zero" case) plus source-text regression checks confirming the wiring sits between PT-C2 and FIN-07, is re-applied inside the max_position_pct cap branch, and is gated to market=="HK" only. Adversarially verified with 3 separate sabotage cycles (removing the PT-C2-adjacent wiring entirely, removing the max_position-cap re-application, breaking lot-size monotonicity) — each caught by the dedicated test(s) targeting exactly that property, reverted and confirmed byte-identical via diff each time. Full 1104-test market-data suite green.',
