    what: 'User asked directly why Total Return showed -99.5%. Live-traced against real production data: 860 real closed SWING trades, genuine 59% win rate, no single trade losing more than ~45%, but the equity-curve math (`equity *= 1 + pct_return/100`, compounded sequentially in entry-date order) implicitly assumed every one of those 860 trades bet 100% of the account, one after another — even though the trades are independent and frequently overlap in time (many SWING positions held concurrently across different symbols). A real, unremarkable 16-trade losing streak (found in the actual data) was enough to compound the "equity" down to ~1% of starting value purely from this all-in assumption, with no relationship to the strategy\'s real quality. Verified the fix\'s effect directly against the same 860-trade sample: at realistic position sizing (10%, ~10 concurrent positions), the same trades produce a genuinely positive total return instead.',
