    implementedNote: 'FIXED 2026-08-14. Tests: new services/market-data/tests/test_squeeze_alert_outcomes.py (22 cases) — real behavioral tests against a real in-memory SQLite session (the established real-sqlalchemy-via-stub-pop-and-restore technique from test_broker_position_sync.py/test_correlation_preentry.py), covering _record_squeeze_alert_outcome()\'s first-fire/no-op/separate-row-per-type/fail-open-on-unknown-symbol behavior, _squeeze_outcome_lookup_price()\'s bisect-nearest-with-grace-window logic, and evaluate_squeeze_alert_outcomes()\'s entry-fill/bullish-win/bearish-win/open-window/never-re-evaluate-a-filled-window/skip-with-no-entry-price behavior — plus source-text checks for the scheduler wiring (recorded before the recipient loop, split by dominant_side, registered as a non-alerting-gated daily cron job) and the admin endpoint (admin-gated, reports all 3 alert types, never merges gamma_unwind_puts with calls). Also added the new "squeeze_alert_outcome_eval_daily" job id to test_alerts_env_gate.py\'s own established _NON_ALERT_JOB_IDS classification list (a pre-existing safety net from BUG-LOCALDEV-ALERTS-UNGATED that would otherwise correctly fail on any newly-registered, unclassified job).\n\nAdversarially verified 3 sabotage/revert cycles, all caught: (1) disabling _record_squeeze_alert_outcome()\'s existence check — initially did NOT fail any test, since the DB\'s own unique constraint caught the resulting duplicate insert and the function\'s fail-open except silently rolled it back, producing the same row count for the wrong reason; strengthened the test to also assert no record_failed warning was logged, which then correctly caught it; (2) flipping evaluate_squeeze_alert_outcomes()\'s bearish-thesis flag to always False — caught by both dedicated gamma_unwind_puts scoring tests; (3) removing the alert_type GROUP BY from the admin endpoint\'s per-window summary query — initially passed because a SIBLING query in the same endpoint (fired_counts) also legitimately groups by alert_type, so a source-text check scoped to the whole function body found it there instead; tightened the test to scope specifically to _summary_for_window()\'s own nested function body, which then correctly caught it. All 3 sabotages reverted and confirmed byte-identical via md5 before moving on. Full 1,341-test market-data suite green; pyflakes clean on all touched backend files (confirmed via git stash that every pre-existing warning predates this change).',
