    implementedNote: 'FIXED 2026-08-15. Tests: services/market-data/tests/test_prebreakout_alert.py gained 6 new cases covering _build_squeeze_family_calibration()/_squeeze_family_calibration_for_alert_type() directly against the real in-memory SQLite session (extended to also create the SqueezeAlertOutcome table/before_insert-id-listener alongside the existing PreBreakoutAlertOutcome setup) — a real bucket for short_squeeze, a real bucket for gamma_unwind_puts using its OWN distinct band scheme (deliberately using a metric value, 62.0, that is only valid under the gamma bands and would fall outside every short_squeeze band entirely — catches a scheme mix-up a shared-value fixture would miss), calls/puts never pooling even at an identical metric value, an unknown alert_type failing open to empty buckets, and a None metric failing open on lookup. New services/market-data/tests/test_squeeze_family_recommendations_wiring.py (18 source-text regression cases, matching test_prebreakout_confidence_wiring.py\'s established pattern for these full DB/Redis/HTTP integration-path functions) covers all 3 fixes\' wiring across all 3 alert functions, including a dedicated test asserting NONE of the 3 functions ever branches (`if`/`elif`) on a regime variable — the structural guarantee that the flag is genuinely soft, not a disguised hard gate. New services/market-data/tests/test_regime_warning_lines.py (9 direct behavioral cases against the real, importable _regime_warning_lines() and all 3 real send_*_email() functions with a captured send_email) confirms bull/None regimes produce silent output, non-bull regimes produce a visible, correctly-worded warning (explicitly checked to never contain "suppressed"/"blocked"/"not sent"/"withheld"), and each of the 3 emails correctly splices it in.\n\nAdversarially verified 4 sabotage/revert cycles against the real scheduler.py/email_service.py, all caught: (1) disabling the short-interest staleness reject in check_prebreakout_alerts() — caught by the dedicated wiring test; (2) hardcoding the gamma calibration lookup to always use "gamma_unwind_calls" regardless of the resolved dominant_side — caught by the dedicated wiring test; (3) removing the alert_type filter from _build_squeeze_family_calibration()\'s own DB query — caught with a real, visible pooling bug (calls_buckets picked up all 40 rows across both sides instead of 30, exactly the "silently cancel real signal" failure mode this test targets); (4) disabling _regime_warning_lines()\'s bull/None early return — caught by exactly the 3 tests exercising that path (the other 6 non-bull-path tests correctly stayed green, confirming the sabotage was isolated to the right code). All 4 sabotages reverted and confirmed byte-identical via md5 before moving on. Full 1,421-test market-data suite green (up from 1,389); pyflakes clean on every touched file (confirmed identical to the pre-existing warning set, zero new warnings introduced).',
