    what: 'The per-signal loop computed entry = _price_at(row.stock_id, sig_date) — the signal\'s OWN calendar date — instead of T+1. Every OTHER entry-price lookup in this same file (and in paper_trading_engine.py\'s _should_enter(), and signal-engine\'s own evaluate_signal_outcomes()) already uses signal_date + timedelta(days=1) for exactly this reason. This one function never received the same treatment.',
    fix: 'entry_date = sig_date + timedelta(days=1); exit_date = entry_date + timedelta(days=hold_days) — matching this file\'s own established entry_price = _nearest_price(row.stock_id, signal_date + timedelta(days=1)) convention used elsewhere at lines 1104/1161/2295. _price_at()\'s own forward-only ("d >= target") nearest-future-price semantics are unchanged.',
    implementedNote: 'FIXED 2026-08-15. New services/signal-engine/tests/test_gate_backtest_lookahead.py (4 cases) — gate_backtest() itself is 250+ lines of DB query construction with cross-service regime-threshold replicas, not easily isolated as a whole (matching test_evaluate_outcomes_nested_savepoint.py\'s own documented reasoning for evaluate_signal_outcomes()); this test instead directly exercises the fixed date-logic and _price_at() lookup via source-text extraction against a real, hand-built price series, proving the actual mechanism the fix uses rather than a hand-copied reimplementation that could drift. Adversarially verified 2 sabotage/revert cycles, both caught: (1) reverting entry_date to the bare sig_date — caught by the dedicated date-logic test; (2) removing _price_at()\'s forward-only guard (d >= target) — initially suspected this might slip past the literal-string test, so a SEPARATE behavioral test (a real 2-price fixture with a gap day) was run against the sabotage directly and correctly caught it via a wrong-price assertion failure (100.0 instead of the correct forward-nearest 105.0), confirming the test exercises real semantic drift, not just literal source text. Both sabotages reverted and confirmed byte-identical via md5 before moving on. Full signal-engine suite green (333 passed, plus the 2 pre-existing, unrelated failure groups already documented elsewhere in this tracker — test_signal_generator.py\'s _decide import-collection error and 4 test_analyst_momentum.py failures, both confirmed via git status to be untouched by this fix); pyflakes clean (confirmed via git stash that the file\'s one pre-existing unused-httpx-import warning predates this change).',
