    impact: 'Medium — user asked to review docs/AUDIT_SHORT_SQUEEZE_2026-07-25.md (a 3-week-old audit) and docs/STRATEGIC_IMPROVEMENT_ROADMAP_2026-07-25.md for trustworthiness before implementing anything. Two parallel research agents verified each document\'s claims directly against current code AND, for the roadmap, against this session\'s own Tier 261-263 measurement-bias audit series. Verdict: the squeeze audit held up completely — all 6 issues and both cheap performance items confirmed STILL genuinely open, zero overlap with anything shipped since; the roadmap did NOT — its headline win-rate numbers traced to a single stale code comment already superseded by Tier 261\'s own verified production numbers, and 4+ of its 8 core proposals (QW-2/3/4, MT-4) turned out to already exist in the codebase under different names. User explicitly deprioritized the roadmap ("only for reference and supplement, not a force to do") and authorized implementing the squeeze audit\'s real findings.',
    what: 'Issue 1: check_short_squeeze_alerts()\'s _fundamentals_cache_misses counter was logged but never exposed anywhere admin-visible — a sustained spike (Redis degradation, the fundamentals-refresh job falling behind) was only visible by reading logs. Issue 2: the 30-day short-interest staleness cutoff (real exchange settlement lag can legitimately make a 30-day-old reading up to ~6 weeks stale) had no intermediate warning — a reading 16-30 days old rendered identically to one 2 days old. Issue 4: the gamma-unwind email\'s 0-DTE "OI as of yesterday\'s close" caveat was inline text only, easy to miss scanning quickly, unlike the existing days_to_cover_critical red-border treatment. Issue 5: check_squeeze_watch_reverts() had NO cache-miss counter at all, unlike its sibling check_short_squeeze_alerts(). Issue 6: squeeze_alert_backtest() couldn\'t distinguish "no stock ever cleared the short-float floor" from "stocks cleared it but never had a qualifying move" when both counts were 0. Perf 4.1: the fundamentals-fetch loop did one Redis GET per symbol inside the candidate loop instead of one batched MGET. Perf 4.3: _build_squeeze_family_calibration()/_build_prebreakout_calibration() ran a fresh DB query every 1-minute cycle even though the underlying outcomes only resolve once daily.',
    fix: 'Issues 1/5: two new rolling-48h Redis counters (_SQUEEZE_FUND_CACHE_MISS_COUNTER_KEY, _SQUEEZE_WATCH_FUND_CACHE_MISS_COUNTER_KEY), reusing the existing _incr_rolling_counter() mechanism already proven for AUD266\'s conviction/fired pair. Surfaced via a new "gauge" _DQ_CHECKS source type (informational only — always ok=True, never enters the failing-list/email-alert path, since a nonzero miss count is expected background noise) — auto-visible on the admin health page via the existing generic /dq-status endpoint with zero new frontend code. Issue 2: new shared _short_interest_age_str() helper (email_service.py) replacing two independently-duplicated age-string implementations, now rendering "moderately stale" (16-21d) / "very stale" (22d+) callouts alongside the existing age display — a visual tier rather than a blind tighten to 21 days, so no currently-firing candidate silently stops alerting with no explanation. Issue 4: the 0-DTE row now gets the same amber-border/⚠️-marker treatment as the existing critical-days-to-cover pattern. Issue 6: squeeze_alert_backtest() now returns reason: "no_qualifying_snapshots" or "no_qualifying_moves" distinguishing the two zero-cases, None otherwise. Perf 4.1: a new price-only pre-pass over stockai:live_prices collects symbols that already clear presence/market-hours/intraday-move filters, then one _rc.mget() call pre-warms every qualifying symbol\'s fundamentals blob before the main candidate loop reads from the pre-warmed dict instead of a fresh GET per symbol. Perf 4.3: new _cached_calibration_buckets(cache_key, builder) wrapper — a 5-minute Redis cache, fail-open to a fresh DB call on any Redis error — wrapping all 4 calibration-builder call sites (short_squeeze, gamma_unwind_calls, gamma_unwind_puts, prebreakout), each with its own distinct cache key.',
    implementedNote: 'FIXED 2026-08-16. Two research agents independently verified both source documents against current code before any implementation began — full verdict recorded in session history: the squeeze audit\'s 6 issues and 2 performance items were all confirmed still genuinely open with zero drift into already-shipped functionality; the roadmap was confirmed unreliable (stale/superseded headline numbers, 4+ proposals already built under different names) and was explicitly set aside per the user\'s own instruction.\n\nTests: new services/market-data/tests/test_squeeze_audit_20260725_fixes.py (32 cases) — _short_interest_age_str() tested directly with real date arithmetic across all 3 tiers and the exact 15/21-day boundaries; send_gamma_unwind_email() tested directly for the 0-DTE badge (including a mixed-batch case confirming the badge is per-row, not email-wide); the admin.py backtest reason field tested via source-text extraction of both zero-cases plus the normal-result None case; the two new rolling counters and the "gauge" DQ-check dispatch branch (confirmed to always report ok=True and never call failing.append, confirmed positioned correctly relative to the "ratio"/"job_status" siblings); the MGET pre-warm pass (confirmed it runs before the MGET call, confirmed the main loop reads from the pre-warmed dict not a fresh Redis call, confirmed Redis-failure fails open to an empty dict, and a dedicated test confirming the two independently-duplicated filter-condition copies use the IDENTICAL threshold constant rather than two literals that could drift apart); and _cached_calibration_buckets() tested directly via source-extraction-plus-exec against fake Redis clients (cache-hit skips the builder entirely, cache-miss calls the builder and writes back with the real 300s TTL read from the real _SQUEEZE_CAL_CACHE_TTL_S constant rather than a hardcoded duplicate, and a Redis-exception case still returns the builder\'s real result).\n\nRefactoring 3 duplicated call sites (Issue 2\'s shared helper, Perf 4.1\'s MGET restructuring, Perf 4.3\'s cache wrapper) broke 3 PRE-EXISTING tests whose literal source-text assertions no longer matched the refactored code shape (test_send_prebreakout_email_renders_short_interest_age, test_short_squeeze_calibration_buckets_are_built_once_before_the_candidate_loop, test_gamma_unwind_calibration_is_built_for_both_calls_and_puts_independently in test_squeeze_family_recommendations_wiring.py; test_calibration_buckets_are_built_once_per_cycle_before_the_candidate_loop in test_prebreakout_confidence_wiring.py; test_cache_miss_counter_is_incremented_before_its_own_continue in test_short_squeeze_alert.py) — all 5 updated to assert against the new, correct code shape rather than the old literal strings, confirmed still testing the same underlying invariant (helper delegation, cache-wrapper presence, build-before-loop ordering, exactly-one-new-call-between-increment-and-continue).\n\nAdversarially verified 4 sabotage/revert cycles, all caught: (1) collapsing the moderately-stale tier boundary in _short_interest_age_str() — caught by exactly the 2 dedicated boundary tests; (2) making the "gauge" DQ-check dispatch branch report a real pass/fail instead of always ok=True — caught by the dedicated dispatch test; (3) making squeeze_alert_backtest()\'s reason always None regardless of candidate_days — caught by 2 of 3 dedicated reason tests (the third, testing the OTHER zero-case, correctly stayed green since it\'s a different code path); (4) diverging the MGET pre-warm pass\'s intraday-move threshold from the main loop\'s own copy — caught by a dedicated duplicated-filter-consistency test added specifically because the two-pass restructuring introduces exactly this drift risk. All 4 sabotages reverted and confirmed byte-identical via md5 before moving on. Full 1,461-test market-data suite green (up from 1,429); pyflakes clean on all 3 touched files (confirmed via git stash that every pre-existing warning predates this change).',
