    implementedNote: 'VERDICT TABLE (verified 2026-08-18, all file:line-cited):\n\n• IF-01 VaR & Stress Testing — PARTIAL (~15%). A live parametric VaR exists (portfolio-optimizer/src/api/risk.py:158-161, one line: port_vol * 1.645) but is request-scoped and NEVER persisted; zero stress testing of any kind.\n• IF-02 Alpha Decay Tracking — NOT BUILT. ⚠️ NAME-COLLISION TRAP: GET /signals/alpha_decay EXISTS but measures a DIFFERENT AXIS (see entry below).\n• IF-03 Earnings Call NLP — NOT BUILT. ⚠️ NAME-COLLISION TRAP: generate_earnings_impact() is an LLM call on NUMERIC EPS/revenue results, never a transcript.\n• IF-04 Cross-Asset Signals — NOT BUILT (narrow partial: spot VIX only). Zero bonds/credit/FX/commodities anywhere.\n• IF-05 Options GEX/Max Pain — NOT BUILT. ⚠️ The existing gamma-unwind alert ALREADY DISCLAIMS in its own source comment that it is not real GEX.\n• IF-06 Smart Order Execution — NOT BUILT. Zero TWAP/VWAP/iceberg; every real order is a market order.\n• IF-07 Factor Exposure — NOT BUILT. ⚠️ NAME-COLLISION TRAP: TWO endpoints named /factor-exposure and /factor_attribution exist; neither is a Fama-French regression.\n• IF-08 Alternative Data — NOT BUILT as designed. Extensive ADJACENT data exists (insider/13F/congress/EDGAR/options flow) but none of the 5 sources the design names.\n• IF-09 Market Microstructure — NOT BUILT. No depth-of-book data source exists in this stack at all.\n• IF-10 Portfolio Attribution — PARTIAL. Real attribution exists but by ENTRY CHARACTERISTIC (score/confidence/regime/RR bands), not Brinson allocation-vs-selection.\n• IF-11 Multi-Strategy — PARTIAL. Capital/P&L isolation genuinely satisfied by the 5-portfolio architecture; DYNAMIC reallocation between them is the real gap.\n• IF-12 Compliance & Audit — PARTIAL. Position/sector/open-risk limits ARE enforced pre-trade in substance; missing the formal rule table, restricted list, and an IMMUTABLE audit trail.\n• IF-13 Regime-Aware Sizing — PARTIAL (largest of the five). A real 5-state regime_size_mult plus 4 stacked dampeners (pre-regime, breadth, HMM, continuous VIX gradient) is live in the sizing formula; volatility TARGETING is genuinely absent and the Kelly endpoint is advisory-only (grep confirms zero consumers).\n\nDOC-SET GAPS FOUND (worth noting for whoever wrote them): the overview table references 7 design docs that do not exist (DESIGN_FACTOR_EXPOSURE.md, DESIGN_ALTERNATIVE_DATA.md, DESIGN_MARKET_MICROSTRUCTURE.md, DESIGN_PORTFOLIO_ATTRIBUTION.md, DESIGN_MULTI_STRATEGY.md, DESIGN_COMPLIANCE_AUDIT.md, DESIGN_REGIME_AWARE_SIZING.md) — IF-07..IF-13 are in fact all covered inside a single unreferenced DESIGN_ADDITIONAL_FEATURES.md, so no content is actually missing, only the filename pointers are wrong.',
