    impact: 'Medium — yield-curve shape and credit spreads are among the most-watched leading indicators for risk appetite and sector rotation, and the app currently has no view of either. Note the app DOES already have a mature regime classifier (bull/neutral/choppy/risk_off/bear, HMM + breadth + VIX), so the honest framing is that this would ENRICH an existing regime/rotation capability rather than create risk-awareness from nothing.',
    what: 'VERIFIED, and the three plausible-looking candidates are each genuinely something else: (1) ML macro features (builder.py:405-530) download exactly THREE tickers — SPY, ^VIX, ^HSI — and DO reach live inference (trainer.py:872, :1246); the only true cross-asset instrument among them is spot VIX. (2) _fetch_overnight_futures (scheduler.py:1821-1893) fetches ES=F/NQ=F/YM=F/RTY=F — all four are EQUITY INDEX futures, and its only consumer is the pre-market brief email (single call site, scheduler.py:2301); it never feeds a signal, score, or gate. (3) FRED (economic.py:49-63) provides 13 macro STATISTICAL series (CPI/PPI/GDP/PAYEMS/FEDFUNDS...) for the release calendar — note FEDFUNDS is the policy rate, NOT a treasury yield curve. Independently confirmed: grep for ^TNX / TLT / HYG / LQD / DXY / T10Y2Y across all services returns ZERO implementation hits. The only "yield_curve_inverted" match is a HARDCODED false literal in an LLM-report fallback scaffold (research-engine routes.py:378,497) that is rendered to users as a checklist row — arguably its own small honesty bug worth fixing regardless.',
    fix: 'Cheapest genuinely-useful slice first, since all the data is free: FRED already has an API key configured in production and serves DGS10/DGS2 (treasury yields) and T10Y2Y (the 2s10s spread) directly — so yield-curve shape is a near-zero-marginal-cost addition to the EXISTING economic.py sync, not a new integration. Credit spreads (BAMLH0A0HYM2) are likewise on FRED. DXY/gold/oil are yfinance tickers. Recommend: (1) extend the existing FRED sync with yields + HY spread; (2) a CrossAssetReading table + daily job; (3) only THEN consider the rule-based RISK_ON/RISK_OFF sector-rotation signals — and gate those behind real validation before letting them influence any live decision, matching this repo\'s standing discipline. Explicitly do NOT wire the hardcoded research-engine yield_curve_inverted literal to real data as a shortcut without also fixing that it currently displays a fabricated value.',
    implementedNote: 'Built 2026-08-19 — the FRED yield-curve piece, exactly the quick win this entry called out. Verified all 5 FRED series IDs live against the real API before hardcoding them (DGS10=4.72%, DGS2=4.19%, T10Y2Y=+0.52%, BAMLH0A0HYM2=2.70%, DTWEXBGS=118.9, all with current dates — not guessed). New CrossAssetReading table (one row per calendar day, all continuous numeric fields — a genuinely different shape from EconomicEvent\'s row-per-release structure), a new sync_cross_asset() reusing sync_fred()\'s exact per-series-isolated fetch pattern, a daily 06:20 UTC scheduler job + startup seed, and GET /events/cross-asset / POST /events/sync/cross-asset routes. get_latest_cross_asset_reading() adds a rule-based RISK_ON/RISK_OFF/NEUTRAL read — explicitly stated as unvalidated macro CONTEXT, not a trading signal, matching this app\'s established CAPE/options-flow-sentiment honesty convention. New CrossAssetCard on intelligence.tsx\'s Overview tab.\n\nDeliberately scoped to FRED-only for this pass — gold/oil (yfinance-sourced) and VIX term structure are a separate follow-on, not added here, to avoid introducing a new cross-service dependency (event-intelligence has no yfinance dependency today) into this first slice.\n\nNew test_cross_asset.py (14 cases) using the established real-in-memory-SQLite-plus-real-model technique. Adversarially verified 3 sabotage cycles: reverting on_conflict_do_update to on_conflict_do_nothing (a real bug — would have silently discarded 4 of every 5 series\' updates to an already-existing day\'s row; caught by 2 tests), flipping the yield-curve-inversion comparison direction (caught by 5 tests), and removing the FRED "." sentinel skip-guard (self-caught "still passes after sabotage" — investigated and found the guard is genuinely redundant against a crash, since float(".") already raises and is caught by the surrounding try/except; the test docstring was corrected to state this precisely rather than over-claim what it proves). Full 270-test event-intelligence suite green; 132-test frontend suite + full next build green; pyflakes clean on all touched files.',
