    what: 'VERIFIED, with the real values (paper_trading_engine.py:4513-4519): regime_size_mult = bull 1.0 / neutral 1.0 / choppy 0.75 / risk_off 0.50 / bear 0.0 — note this is a 5-state vocabulary (not the design\'s bull/high_vol/bear/crisis) and BEAR IS 0.0 (no entry at all), materially stricter than the design\'s proposed 0.4. Four further dampeners stack via min(): pre-regime early warning, market breadth vs 200EMA, HMM bear pressure, and a CONTINUOUS VIX gradient (1.0 - (vix-20)/30, floored at 0.5). Independently confirmed: zero matches for target_vol/vol_target/volatility_target; and grep for "kelly" in paper_trading_engine.py + decision-engine sizer.py returned ZERO before this fix — GET /paper-portfolio/kelly computes quarter-Kelly and a recommended_risk_pct but NOTHING consumed it for actual sizing. It was advisory-only, and also not regime-adjusted.',
    fix: 'Two pieces. (1) VOLATILITY TARGETING (built first) — a target_vol/realized_vol ratio multiplier, clamped [0.5, 1.5], applied as its own genuine multiply of regime_size_mult (not a further min() — every OTHER dampener inside regime_size_mult composes downward-only via min(), but vol-targeting must be able to move sizing UP when realized vol is comfortably below target). (2) KELLY-CONSUMPTION — presented 3 options via AskUserQuestion (wire in with a validation gate / wire in unvalidated / document as intentionally advisory-only); user explicitly chose the validated-gate option. Built a new walk-forward sweep (sweep_risk_per_trade_pct(), portfolio_backtest.py) reusing the SAME day-stepped multi-symbol simulator and chronological 70/30 train/validation + promotion-margin discipline already proven for sweep_max_portfolio_drawdown_pct() — candidates are Kelly\'s own real recommended_risk_pct bands (1%/2%/3%, not an independently-guessed grid) plus the current live value. Promotion metric is total_return_pct (not max_drawdown_pct alone, matching the sibling sweep\'s own reasoning — a risk level tuned purely to minimize drawdown trivially wins by sizing every position to nothing). New GET /paper-portfolio/backtest/risk-per-trade-sweep route (admin-only, read-only research signal — never an automatic capital-sizing change), correctly threading HK\'s own real 0.007 default (not the US 0.01) as the comparison baseline when market=HK.',
    implementedNote: 'Built 2026-08-19/20 across two passes. Volatility-targeting half: new _compute_portfolio_vol_targeting_mult(session, portfolio_id) computes annualized realized volatility from the SAME PaperEquityCurve daily-return formula _portfolio_risk_metrics() already uses, reusing its own _MIN_SHARPE_DAYS=20 sample floor so a too-short curve fails open to a neutral 1.0. Gated behind a new vol_targeting_enabled cfg flag (default True). Tests: test_vol_targeting.py (11 cases) — sample-floor/zero-variance fail-open, both clamp directions, per-portfolio isolation, 3 source-text checks (multiply-not-min, admin toggle, neutral-multiplier log suppression). Kelly-consumption half: sweep_risk_per_trade_pct() reuses run_portfolio_backtest() as its replay primitive (see that module\'s own top-of-file honest-scope docstring for exactly what is and is not modeled — no decision-engine/_should_enter() replay, no aggregate open-risk cap, no correlation cap, no commission/slippage). Tests: 7 new cases in test_portfolio_backtest.py\'s TestSweepRiskPerTradePct (Kelly-band candidate defaults, HK-specific base-value respect, a genuinely-promotable higher-risk%-improves-return scenario since shares scale linearly with risk_per_trade_pct per _size_position()\'s own risk_dollar/stop_distance formula, and a dedicated SD-ratio-guard test mirroring the drawdown sweep\'s own equivalent) + 9 source-text route-wiring tests in test_backtest_risk_per_trade_sweep_route.py. A REAL SELF-CAUGHT GAP during adversarial verification: the first version of TestSweepRiskPerTradePct had no test asserting a SHOULD-fail scenario actually fails — sabotaging the promotion-margin gate to hardcode promoted=True passed every existing test in the class undetected (the "still passes after sabotage" red flag this repo\'s own testing discipline treats as a finding in its own right). Fixed by adding a dedicated SD-ratio test mirroring the drawdown sweep\'s own established isolation technique (a huge win identical under both candidate/baseline inflates the combined SD without touching the lift) — required real trial-and-error on the exact candidate risk% gap (0.01 vs 0.03 produced too large a lift given risk_per_trade_pct\'s linear effect on dollar P&L; settled on 0.0100 vs 0.0105 to land a lift just above the absolute floor but still SD-guard-rejectable). Adversarially verified 3 sabotage/revert cycles total, all caught and confirmed byte-identical via md5sum after restoring: (1) hardcoding promoted=True — caught only after the SD-ratio test fix; (2) inverting the best-candidate selection to pick the WORST train-slice performer — caught by 2 tests; (3) removing the API route\'s HK-specific base_cfg_overrides passthrough — caught by a dedicated wiring test. Full 1909-test market-data suite green; pyflakes clean on both touched files (portfolio_backtest.py fully clean; paper_portfolio.py\'s 4 pre-existing warnings unchanged).',
