    impact: 'Low — training-pipeline debuggability only, never a live-trading-affecting path. A silent `except Exception: pass`/`return []` swallows a real failure (a malformed price series, a missing macro feature, a corrupted model file) with zero trace, making a training run that silently under-performed indistinguishable from one that ran cleanly.',
    what: 'Confirmed via direct grep + read: 35 total `except Exception` blocks (trainer.py 21, tuner.py 6, meta_trainer.py 8 — the audit\'s count is exact). Of these, 6 ALREADY logged via a real log.warning(...) call before continuing (trainer.py:532,643; tuner.py:96; meta_trainer.py:185,447,596) — the audit\'s grep matched the bare `except Exception:` line without checking whether the block\'s body actually logs, overstating the truly-silent count by these 6. 2 more (both model-save atomic-write blocks in trainer.py/meta_trainer.py, RACE-001) were confirmed already fail-CLOSED via a bare `raise` — correctly propagating, not silent. The remaining ~29 were genuinely silent — no log call anywhere in the except block.',
    fix: 'Not a blanket find-and-replace (the audit\'s own proposed fix) — went through each of the ~29 individually, choosing a real judgment call per site rather than mechanically wrapping every except in an identical log.warning call: symbol-scoped log.warning for real per-symbol failures (fundamentals/macro/sector/outcome-feature fetches, model-save reads, ensemble-member predictions), log.debug for per-window skips inside validate_walkforward()\'s potentially-long loop (matching this file\'s own established convention of not spamming warning-level logs for expected-frequency events), and one deliberately left as a bare raise (RACE-001\'s atomic model-save, already correctly fail-closed, needed no change).',
    implementedNote: 'Built 2026-08-26. The single highest-value fix in this pass: predict_latest_ensemble_three()\'s meta-model prediction call (trainer.py) — its OWN existing comment already documents a real, previously-undiscovered bug (T237-ML-META3: a bare, unimported module name that raised ModuleNotFoundError on EVERY call, completely silently, for a long time) that this exact except block\'s silence is what hid. The fix adds a dedicated log line there specifically so a regression of that class can never go unnoticed again — the missing log line is literally what let the original bug hide. 21 sites fixed across trainer.py (fundamentals/macro/sector/outcome-feature loads in both train and inference paths, feature-attribution failures, RF/LGB/meta ensemble-member fallbacks, per-window walk-forward skips), 5 in tuner.py (the same macro/sector/outcome/fundamentals/fund-snapshots enrichment-fetch pattern as trainer.py, same fix), 2 in meta_trainer.py (macro-features in both the training-mining loop and predict_meta(), plus a build_features() per-symbol failure in the mining loop). Verified via direct AST-adjacent scanning of every except-Exception block in all 3 files, not just a spot-check, before considering this complete. Full 91-test ml-prediction suite green (zero regressions); pyflakes clean (all 3 remaining warnings — db.Signal/SECTOR_COLUMNS/sqlalchemy.select imported-but-unused — confirmed pre-existing via git stash, none newly introduced by this fix).',
