    what: 'Found while sweeping logs across all 12 backend services during EC2 reboot recovery (unrelated to the reboot itself). Traced the full traceback: routes.py:85, `game_plan = {k: float(v) for k, v in req.game_plan.items()}`, raised a raw ValueError("could not convert string to float: \'GROWTH\'"). paper_trading_engine.py\'s _build_game_plan_for_style() (the ONLY real caller of this endpoint with a non-empty game_plan — decide.tsx never sends one, always taking the abuild_game_plan() branch instead) legitimately returns a dict with a "style" key (a string like "GROWTH") alongside the numeric entry1/entry2/breakout/stop/take_profit/current_price fields — this bug has existed since decision-engine was first built (Tier 57, commit 5871ebc) and was never caught because most real candidates never reach this call site (filtered out by earlier gates first) — only ~3 per 24h actually trigger it, against a background of ~660 real 200s in the same window, which is why it went unnoticed this long.',
