    what: 'The scheduler.py-alerts half of the survey interrupted earlier by the org spend limit, resumed and re-verified directly against current code. Confirmed via CLAUDE.md that AUD256 fixed exactly send_premarket_brief/send_morning_digest, and that Tier 266\'s own 2026-08-05 doc-only audit explicitly flagged "the other 7 alert loops still lack [this]" as FUTURE work, never shipped. Re-checked all ~24 candidate multi-recipient loops directly: nearly all of them (check_volume_anomalies, check_short_squeeze_alerts, check_squeeze_ignition_alerts, check_prebreakout_alerts, check_gamma_unwind_alerts, check_value_area_breakdown, check_top3_conviction, check_signal_alerts, check_price_alerts, check_technical_alerts, check_earnings_beat_screener_alerts, check_portfolio_drawdown_alerts, send_weekly_theme_forecast, send_weekly_trade_coach, check_sector_rotation_alerts, check_early_earnings_news_alerts) have SINCE received the fix under their own AUD266 tags, closing most of Tier 266\'s own backlog quietly. Exactly 2 genuine gaps remained: send_post_open_digest() (market/window post-open update email, scheduler.py:8515) had neither half of the pattern at all; send_paper_portfolio_digest() (scheduler.py:9334) also had neither half, PLUS re-executed its own `portfolios` query once per user for no reason (the query has no per-user filter -- every user gets the identical active-portfolio list), a pure redundant-query waste found while restructuring the same loop.',
    fix: 'Ported the exact AUD256/send_morning_digest pattern to both functions: a per-(user, market, window, date) / per-(user, portfolio, date) Redis dedup key checked before the send and set only after a confirmed successful send, plus a dedicated try/except around the send call. For send_paper_portfolio_digest() specifically, the try/except was widened to wrap the ENTIRE per-portfolio block (risk-metrics computation + trade queries + send), not just the send call, matching the wider blast-radius this specific loop\'s own structure demanded. Also hoisted the redundant `portfolios` query to run exactly once, before the outer per-user loop, since its result never depends on which user is currently being emailed.',
    implementedNote: 'Fixed 2026-08-24. New services/market-data/tests/test_post_open_and_paper_portfolio_digest_send_loop.py (11 cases, source-text extraction matching test_morning_digest_send_loop.py\'s established pattern -- scheduler.py can\'t be imported directly in this test environment): dedup-checked-before-send, dedup-key-set-only-after-success, per-recipient error isolation, errors logged+counted without re-raising, dedup key correctly scoped (per market+window for post_open_digest; per user+portfolio for paper_portfolio_digest, so a user with 2 active portfolios still gets 2 separate digests), and the redundant-query fix (queried exactly once, before the outer loop). A real, self-caught test-quality bug found and fixed DURING adversarial verification: the first version of the paper_portfolio isolation test used a naive `.rindex("try:", 0, metrics_call_idx)` to find the wrapping try block -- sabotaging the real fix (removing the per-portfolio try/except entirely) did NOT fail this test, because the search silently fell back to an unrelated, earlier function-level try block that also happened to precede the metrics call. Fixed by anchoring the test on the exact structural adjacency between the dedup-check\'s own closing except and the per-portfolio isolation try\'s opening clause immediately after it -- a marker that can only exist if the real fix is genuinely present. Re-verified: the corrected test now fails with a clear ValueError when the fix is removed, rather than silently passing. Adversarially verified 3 sabotage cycles total, all caught and reverted: the corrected isolation-scope test (above), removing the post_open_digest dedup check entirely (caught by 2 dedicated tests), and re-introducing the per-user redundant portfolios query (caught by the dedicated query-count test). Full 2004-test market-data suite green (up from 1993); pyflakes clean (all 4 pre-existing warnings confirmed via git stash to predate this change).',
