    what: 'Section 4.3 of docs/recomm_or_audit/REALTIME_NEWS_EVENTS_INTELLIGENCE_2025-08-22.md (already reviewed once this session -- Tier 299) proposed a 6-section Market Pulse Dashboard as a P0 item. Before building, verified it was not already a duplicate of the existing MarketPulseCard on intelligence.tsx (T249-MARKETMOVER-P4, built 2026-07-18) -- confirmed that card is narrow (headlines + a sentiment score + themes only), and separately confirmed index.tsx\'s "Dashboard" is a watchlist-management console (add/remove stocks, per-stock signals, ingestion controls), not a market-wide overview -- neither page already covers this. Also independently re-verified the doc\'s OWN "4.1 FOMO Composite Score" companion proposal before considering it too: its formula assumes a live, callable, per-symbol 0-100 squeeze_score exists ("all inputs exist") -- traced this directly into scheduler.py and found squeeze scoring only exists as a calibration-bucket lookup keyed to already-fired alerts (_build_squeeze_family_calibration), never a general reusable per-symbol score -- the doc\'s claim did not hold up, so the FOMO score was dropped from this build rather than composed on a false premise. For the dashboard\'s own 6 sections, individually verified each one\'s real backing data before writing any UI: regime (api.regime + api.fearGreed, both real), macro events today (api.eventsCalendar filtered to macro-only types), top movers and sector heat map (both derivable client-side from ONE existing api.sectorPerformance() call -- its SectorGroup[].stocks[] already carries per-stock change_pct, so no new backend endpoint was needed for either section), news pulse (reuses api.marketPulse() + the existing NewsCard component), and active alerts (admin-only bonus section -- the only "recently fired alerts" feed that actually exists is api.getSqueezeAlertPerformance()\'s recent_alerts field, narrower than the doc\'s "all alert types" framing but real).',
