    what: 'A background survey of ml-prediction/ranking-engine validation gaps found this as the one genuine, currently-unfixed finding after checking many already-fixed candidates. `xgb_auc = float((xgb.get("metrics") or {}).get("auc") or ... or 0.55)` -- Python\'s `or` treats a real, legitimate auc=0.0 (a perfectly rank-inverted model, rare but real) as falsy and silently substitutes 0.55, giving a degenerate model near-normal ensemble weight instead of the ~zero weight it deserves. Separately, a model already flagged oos_suppressed=True by predict_latest() (CV-AUC < 0.52, coin-flip territory -- predict_latest() already neutralizes that model\'s OWN bullish_probability to 0.5) still had its own real held-out AUC feed this weighting formula at full strength; the top-level oos_suppressed flag on the returned dict only informs signal-engine\'s downstream SA-27 compression AFTER the blend already happened. The sibling 3-model ensemble function, predict_latest_ensemble_three(), already received the equivalent oos_suppressed exclusion under T237-ML1 -- this 2-model fallback never did. Confirmed reachable: POST /ml/predict_ensemble\'s mean_model_test_auc is consumed again with the identical or-pattern at signal-engine/generators/signals.py:402, driving the ML/TA fusion weight.',
    fix: '_model_auc()/_model_thr() helpers use `is not None` (the correct presence check -- the 0.55/0.5 fallback should only fire when the metric is genuinely absent, never merely equal to 0). A suppressed model\'s AUC is zeroed out for weighting purposes, with a rescue path for both-suppressed (restore real AUCs rather than leave zero total weight) and a further rescue for the edge case where NEITHER model is suppressed but both happen to report a real auc=0.0 (no meaningful AUC signal to weight by -- split evenly rather than divide by zero or fabricate a preference). The returned metrics.cv_auc_mean field now reads each model\'s OWN real cv_auc_mean via a separate _cv_auc_mean() helper -- reusing the (possibly-zeroed-for-suppression) weighting values here would have misreported a suppressed model\'s real CV AUC as 0.0 to any caller reading this diagnostic field.',
